# Chess Endgame Practice App - Mate in 1

Here's a complete chess endgame practice app with 3 mate-in-1 scenarios, drag-and-drop functionality, and visual feedback:

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>Chess Endgame Practice - Mate in 1</title>
    <style>
        * {
            margin: 0;
            padding: 0;
            box-sizing: border-box;
        }

        body {
            font-family: 'Segoe UI', Tahoma, Geneva, Verdana, sans-serif;
            background: linear-gradient(135deg, #1a1a2e 0%, #16213e 100%);
            min-height: 100vh;
            display: flex;
            justify-content: center;
            align-items: center;
            padding: 20px;
            color: white;
        }

        .container {
            text-align: center;
        }

        h1 {
            margin-bottom: 10px;
            font-size: 2rem;
            text-shadow: 2px 2px 4px rgba(0,0,0,0.5);
        }

        h2 {
            margin-bottom: 20px;
            font-size: 1.2rem;
            color: #78e08f;
        }

        .controls {
            margin-bottom: 20px;
            display: flex;
            flex-wrap: wrap;
            justify-content: center;
            gap: 10px;
        }

        .scenario-btn, .reset-btn {
            padding: 12px 24px;
            font-size: 16px;
            cursor: pointer;
            border: none;
            border-radius: 8px;
            transition: all 0.3s;
            font-weight: 600;
        }

        .scenario-btn {
            background: #4a69bd;
            color: white;
        }

        .scenario-btn:hover {
            background: #6a89cc;
            transform: translateY(-2px);
        }

        .scenario-btn.active {
            background: #78e08f;
            color: #1a1a2e;
        }

        .reset-btn {
            background: #eb4d4b;
            color: white;
        }

        .reset-btn:hover {
            background: #ff6b6b;
            transform: translateY(-2px);
        }

        .board-container {
            display: inline-block;
            padding: 15px;
            background: #2c3e50;
            border-radius: 12px;
            box-shadow: 0 15px 40px rgba(0,0,0,0.5);
        }

        .file-labels, .rank-labels {
            display: flex;
            font-size: 14px;
            color: #95a5a6;
        }

        .file-labels {
            justify-content: space-around;
            padding: 5px 25px;
        }

        .file-labels span {
            width: 60px;
            text-align: center;
        }

        .board-wrapper {
            display: flex;
        }

        .rank-labels {
            flex-direction: column;
            justify-content: space-around;
            padding: 0 8px;
        }

        .rank-labels span {
            height: 60px;
            display: flex;
            align-items: center;
        }

        .board {
            display: grid;
            grid-template-columns: repeat(8, 60px);
            grid-template-rows: repeat(8, 60px);
            border: 3px solid #34495e;
        }

        .square {
            width: 60px;
            height: 60px;
            display: flex;
            justify-content: center;
            align-items: center;
            font-size: 45px;
            cursor: pointer;
            user-select: none;
            position: relative;
            transition: background 0.2s;
        }

        .white-square {
            background: #f0d9b5;
        }

        .black-square {
            background: #b58863;
        }

        .square.valid-move::after {
            content: '';
            position: absolute;
            width: 20px;
            height: 20px;
            background: rgba(100, 200, 100, 0.7);
            border-radius: 50%;
        }

        .square.valid-move.has-piece::after {
            width: 100%;
            height: 100%;
            border-radius: 0;
            background: rgba(255, 100, 100, 0.4);
        }

        .square.highlight {
            box-shadow: inset 0 0 0 4px rgba(255, 255, 0, 0.8);
        }

        .square.last-move {
            background: rgba(255, 255, 0, 0.3);
        }

        .white-square.last-move {
            background: #e8d174;
        }

        .black-square.last-move {
            background: #a89050;
        }

        .piece {
            cursor: grab;
            transition: transform 0.1s;
        }

        .piece:active {
            cursor: grabbing;
        }

        .piece.dragging {
            opacity: 0.4;
        }

        .piece.white-piece {
            color: #fff;
            text-shadow: 0 0 3px #000, 0 0 3px #000;
        }

        .piece.black-piece {
            color: #000;
            text-shadow: 0 0 2px #fff;
        }

        .status {
            margin-top: 20px;
            font-size: 22px;
            font-weight: bold;
            min-height: 35px;
            transition: all 0.3s;
        }

        .status.success {
            color: #78e08f;
            animation: pulse 0.5s ease-in-out;
        }

        .status.error {
            color: #ff6b6b;
            animation: shake 0.4s ease-in-out;
        }

        .status.info {
            color: #74b9ff;
        }

        @keyframes pulse {
            0%, 100% { transform: scale(1); }
            50% { transform: scale(1.1); }
        }

        @keyframes shake {
            0%, 100% { transform: translateX(0); }
            25% { transform: translateX(-10px); }
            75% { transform: translateX(10px); }
        }

        .description {
            margin-top: 15px;
            font-size: 15px;
            color: #bdc3c7;
            max-width: 500px;
            margin-left: auto;
            margin-right: auto;
            line-height: 1.5;
        }

        .scenario-name {
            font-weight: bold;
            color: #f39c12;
            font-size: 16px;
            margin-bottom: 5px;
        }

        /* Checkmate Overlay */
        .checkmate-overlay {
            position: fixed;
            top: 0;
            left: 0;
            width: 100%;
            height: 100%;
            background: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.85);
            display: flex;
            justify-content: center;
            align-items: center;
            z-index: 1000;
            opacity: 0;
            pointer-events: none;
            transition: opacity 0.5s;
        }

        .checkmate-overlay.show {
            opacity: 1;
            pointer-events: auto;
        }

        .checkmate-content {
            background: linear-gradient(135deg, #2c3e50 0%, #1a252f 100%);
            padding: 50px 70px;
            border-radius: 20px;
            text-align: center;
            box-shadow: 0 25px 80px rgba(0,0,0,0.6);
            border: 3px solid #78e08f;
            animation: scaleIn 0.5s ease-out;
        }

        .checkmate-overlay.show .checkmate-content {
            animation: scaleIn 0.5s ease-out, glow 2s ease-in-out infinite;
        }

        @keyframes scaleIn {
            from { transform: scale(0.5); opacity: 0; }
            to { transform: scale(1); opacity: 1; }
        }

        @keyframes glow {
            0%, 100% { box-shadow: 0 0 20px rgba(120, 224, 143, 0.3); }
            50% { box-shadow: 0 0 40px rgba(120, 224, 143, 0.6); }
        }

        .checkmate-content h2 {
            font-size: 42px;
            color: #78e08f;
            margin-bottom: 15px;
        }

        .checkmate-content .trophy {
            font-size: 80px;
            margin-bottom: 20px;
            animation: bounce 1s ease-in-out infinite;
        }

        @keyframes bounce {
            0%, 100% { transform: translateY(0); }
            50% { transform: translateY(-10px); }
        }

        .checkmate-content p {
            font-size: 18px;
            margin-bottom: 30px;
            color: #bdc3c7;
        }

        .overlay-buttons {
            display: flex;
            gap: 15px;
            justify-content: center;
        }

        .overlay-btn {
            padding: 15px 35px;
            font-size: 16px;
            font-weight: 600;
            border: none;
            border-radius: 10px;
            cursor: pointer;
            transition: all 0.3s;
        }

        .continue-btn {
            background: #78e08f;
            color: #1a1a2e;
        }

        .continue-btn:hover {
            background: #9aecb0;
            transform: translateY(-2px);
        }

        .next-btn {
            background: #4a69bd;
            color: white;
        }

        .next-btn:hover {
            background: #6a89cc;
            transform: translateY(-2px);
        }

        /* Move counter */
        .move-counter {
            margin-top: 10px;
            font-size: 14px;
            color: #7f8c8d;
        }
    </style>
</head>
<body>
    <div class="container">
        <h1>♟️ Chess Endgame Practice</h1>
        <h2>White to Play - Mate in 1</h2>

        <div class="controls">
            <button class="scenario-btn active" onclick="loadScenario(1)">Scenario 1</button>
            <button class="scenario-btn" onclick="loadScenario(2)">Scenario 2</button>
            <button class="scenario-btn" onclick="loadScenario(3)">Scenario 3</button>
            <button class="reset-btn" onclick="resetPosition()">🔄 Reset</button>
        </div>

        <div class="board-container">
            <div class="file-labels">
                <span>a</span><span>b</span><span>c</span><span>d</span>
                <span>e</span><span>f</span><span>g</span><span>h</span>
            </div>
            <div class="board-wrapper">
                <div class="rank-labels">
                    <span>8</span><span>7</span><span>6</span><span>5</span>
                    <span>4</span><span>3</span><span>2</span><span>1</span>
                </div>
                <div class="board" id="board"></div>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="status" id="status"></div>
        <div class="scenario-name" id="scenarioName"></div>
        <div class="description" id="description"></div>
        <div class="move-counter" id="moveCounter"></div>
    </div>

    <div class="checkmate-overlay" id="overlay">
        <div class="checkmate-content">
            <div class="trophy">🏆</div>
            <h2>CHECKMATE!</h2>
            <p id="successMessage">Excellent! You found the winning move!</p>
            <div class="overlay-buttons">
                <button class="overlay-btn continue-btn" onclick="closeOverlay()">Continue</button>
                <button class="overlay-btn next-btn" onclick="nextScenario()">Next Puzzle →</button>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>

    <script>
        // Chess piece Unicode symbols
        const PIECES = {
            'K': '♔', 'Q': '♕', 'R': '♖', 'B': '♗', 'N': '♘', 'P': '♙',
            'k': '♚', 'q': '♛', 'r': '♜', 'b': '♝', 'n': '♞', 'p': '♟'
        };

        // Mate in 1 Scenarios
        const scenarios = {
            1: {
                name: "Back Rank Mate",
                description: "The black king is trapped behind its own pawns. Use your rook to deliver checkmate on the back rank! Hint: Control the 8th rank.",
                position: [
                    [null, null, null, null, null, null, 'k', null],
                    [null, null, null, null, null, 'p', 'p', 'p'],
                    [null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null],
                    [null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null],
                    [null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null],
                    [null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null],
                    [null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null],
                    ['R', null, null, null, null, null, 'K', null]
                ]
            },
            2: {
                name: "Queen Delivery Mate",
                description: "The black king is cornered with pawns blocking its escape. Find the queen move that delivers checkmate! The king has nowhere to run.",
                position: [
                    [null, null, null, null, null, null, null, 'k'],
                    [null, null, null, null, null, null, 'p', 'p'],
                    [null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null],
                    [null, null, null, null, null, 'Q', null, null],
                    [null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null],
                    [null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null],
                    [null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null],
                    [null, null, null, null, null, null, 'K', null]
                ]
            },
            3: {
                name: "King & Rook Coordination",
                description: "Your king and rook work together to trap the enemy king on the edge. The white king cuts off escape squares. Find the mating move!",
                position: [
                    [null, null, null, null, null, 'k', null, null],
                    ['R', null, null, null, null, null, null, null],
                    [null, null, null, null, null, 'K', null, null],
                    [null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null],
                    [null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null],
                    [null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null],
                    [null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null],
                    [null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null]
                ]
            }
        };

        // Game state
        let currentScenario = 1;
        let board = [];
        let draggedPiece = null;
        let dragStartSquare = null;
        let moveAttempts = 0;
        let lastMove = null;

        // Initialize the app
        function init() {
            loadScenario(1);
        }

        // Load a scenario
        function loadScenario(num) {
            currentScenario = num;
            board = JSON.parse(JSON.stringify(scenarios[num].position));
            moveAttempts = 0;
            lastMove = null;

            // Update button states
            document.querySelectorAll('.scenario-btn').forEach((btn, i) => {
                btn.classList.toggle('active', i + 1 === num);
            });

            // Update info displays
            document.getElementById('scenarioName').textContent = scenarios[num].name;
            document.getElementById('description').textContent = scenarios[num].description;
            document.getElementById('status').textContent = '';
            document.getElementById('status').className = 'status';
            updateMoveCounter();

            renderBoard();
        }

        // Reset current position
        function resetPosition() {
            loadScenario(currentScenario);
            showStatus("Position reset. Try again!", "info");
        }

        // Update move counter display
        function updateMoveCounter() {
            document.getElementById('moveCounter').textContent = `Attempts: ${moveAttempts}`;
        }

        // Render the chess board
        function renderBoard() {
            const boardEl = document.getElementById('board');
            boardEl.innerHTML = '';

            for (let row = 0; row < 8; row++) {
                for (let col = 0; col < 8; col++) {
                    const square = document.createElement('div');
                    const isWhiteSquare = (row + col) % 2 === 0;
                    square.className = `square ${isWhiteSquare ? 'white-square' : 'black-square'}`;
                    square.dataset.row = row;
                    square.dataset.col = col;

                    // Highlight last move
                    if (lastMove && 
                        ((lastMove.from.row === row && lastMove.from.col === col) ||
                         (lastMove.to.row === row && lastMove.to.col === col))) {
                        square.classList.add('last-move');
                    }

                    const piece = board[row][col];
                    if (piece) {
                        square.textContent = PIECES[piece];
                        square.classList.add('piece');
                        square.classList.add(isWhitePiece(piece) ? 'white-piece' : 'black-piece');

                        // Only white pieces are draggable
                        if (isWhitePiece(piece)) {
                            square.draggable = true;
                            square.addEventListener('dragstart', handleDragStart);
                            square.addEventListener('dragend', handleDragEnd);
                        }
                    }

                    // Drop zone events
                    square.addEventListener('dragover', handleDragOver);
                    square.addEventListener('drop', handleDrop);
                    square.addEventListener('dragenter', handleDragEnter);
                    square.addEventListener('dragleave', handleDragLeave);

                    boardEl.appendChild(square);
                }
            }
        }

        // Drag start handler
        function handleDragStart(e) {
            const row = parseInt(e.target.dataset.row);
            const col = parseInt(e.target.dataset.col);

            dragStartSquare = { row, col };
            draggedPiece = board[row][col];

            e.target.classList.add('dragging');
            e.dataTransfer.effectAllowed = 'move';
            e.dataTransfer.setData('text/plain', '');

            // Show valid moves after a brief delay (for visual smoothness)
            setTimeout(() => highlightValidMoves(row, col), 10);
        }

        // Drag end handler
        function handleDragEnd(e) {
            e.target.classList.remove('dragging');
            clearHighlights();
        }

        // Drag over handler
        function handleDragOver(e) {
            e.preventDefault();
            e.dataTransfer.dropEffect = 'move';
        }

        // Drag enter handler
        function handleDragEnter(e) {
            e.preventDefault();
            const square = e.target.closest('.square');
            if (square && !square.classList.contains('dragging')) {
                square.classList.add('highlight');
            }
        }

        // Drag leave handler
        function handleDragLeave(e) {
            const square = e.target.closest('.square');
            if (square) {
                square.classList.remove('highlight');
            }
        }

        // Drop handler
        function handleDrop(e) {
            e.preventDefault();
            const square = e.target.closest('.square');
            if (!square) return;

            square.classList.remove('highlight');

            const toRow = parseInt(square.dataset.row);
            const toCol = parseInt(square.dataset.col);

            if (dragStartSquare && draggedPiece) {
                attemptMove(dragStartSquare.row, dragStartSquare.col, toRow, toCol);
            }

            clearHighlights();
            dragStartSquare = null;
            draggedPiece = null;
        }

        // Highlight valid move squares
        function highlightValidMoves(fromRow, fromCol) {
            const piece = board[fromRow][fromCol];
            if (!piece) return;

            const squares = document.querySelectorAll('.square');

            for (let row = 0; row < 8; row++) {
                for (let col = 0; col < 8; col++) {
                    if (isValidMove(piece, fromRow, fromCol, row, col)) {
                        const index = row * 8 + col;
                        squares[index].classList.add('valid-move');
                        if (board[row][col]) {
                            squares[index].classList.add('has-piece');
                        }
                    }
                }
            }
        }

        // Clear all highlights
        function clearHighlights() {
            document.querySelectorAll('.square').forEach(sq => {
                sq.classList.remove('valid-move', 'highlight', 'has-piece');
            });
        }

        // Check if move is valid for the piece type
        function isValidMove(piece, fromRow, fromCol, toRow, toCol) {
            // Can't stay in place
            if (fromRow === toRow && fromCol === toCol) return false;

            // Can't capture own piece
            const targetPiece = board[toRow][toCol];
            if (targetPiece && isWhitePiece(piece) === isWhitePiece(targetPiece)) return false;

            const pieceType = piece.toUpperCase();
            const rowDiff = Math.abs(toRow - fromRow);
            const colDiff = Math.abs(toCol - fromCol);

            switch (pieceType) {
                case 'K':
                    return rowDiff <= 1 && colDiff <= 1;

                case 'Q':
                    return (fromRow === toRow || fromCol === toCol || rowDiff === colDiff) && 
                           isPathClear(fromRow, fromCol, toRow, toCol);

                case 'R':
                    return (fromRow === toRow || fromCol === toCol) && 
                           isPathClear(fromRow, fromCol, toRow, toCol);

                case 'B':
                    return rowDiff === colDiff && isPathClear(fromRow, fromCol, toRow, toCol);

                case 'N':
                    return (rowDiff === 2 && colDiff === 1) || (rowDiff === 1 && colDiff === 2);

                case 'P':
                    const direction = isWhitePiece(piece) ? -1 : 1;
                    const startRow = isWhitePiece(piece) ? 6 : 1;

                    // Forward move
                    if (colDiff === 0 && !targetPiece) {
                        if (toRow === fromRow + direction) return true;
                        if (fromRow === startRow && toRow === fromRow + 2 * direction && !board[fromRow + direction][fromCol]) return true;
                    }
                    // Capture
                    if (colDiff === 1 && toRow === fromRow + direction && targetPiece) return true;
                    return false;
            }

            return false;
        }

        // Check if path is clear for sliding pieces
        function isPathClear(fromRow, fromCol, toRow, toCol) {
            const rowDir = Math.sign(toRow - fromRow);
            const colDir = Math.sign(toCol - fromCol);

            let r = fromRow + rowDir;
            let c = fromCol + colDir;

            while (r !== toRow || c !== toCol) {
                if (board[r][c]) return false;
                r += rowDir;
                c += colDir;
            }

            return true;
        }

        // Check if piece is white
        function isWhitePiece(piece) {
            return piece === piece.toUpperCase();
        }

        // Attempt to make a move
        function attemptMove(fromRow, fromCol, toRow, toCol) {
            const piece = board[fromRow][fromCol];

            if (!piece || !isWhitePiece(piece)) {
                showStatus("You can only move white pieces!", "error");
                return;
            }

            if (!isValidMove(piece, fromRow, fromCol, toRow, toCol)) {
                showStatus("Invalid move for this piece!", "error");
                return;
            }

            moveAttempts++;
            updateMoveCounter();

            // Make the move temporarily
            const capturedPiece = board[toRow][toCol];
            board[toRow][toCol] = piece;
            board[fromRow][fromCol] = null;

            // Store last move for highlighting
            lastMove = { from: { row: fromRow, col: fromCol }, to: { row: toRow, col: toCol } };

            // Check result
            if (isCheckmate()) {
                renderBoard();
                showCheckmate();
            } else if (isKingInCheck(false)) {
                showStatus("Check! But not checkmate. Try again!", "error");
                // Undo move
                board[fromRow][fromCol] = piece;
                board[toRow][toCol] = capturedPiece;
                lastMove = null;
                renderBoard();
            } else {
                showStatus("Not checkmate. The king can escape! Try again.", "error");
                // Undo move
                board[fromRow][fromCol] = piece;
                board[toRow][toCol] = capturedPiece;
                lastMove = null;
                renderBoard();
            }
        }

        // Find king position
        function findKing(isWhite) {
            const kingChar = isWhite ? 'K' : 'k';
            for (let row = 0; row < 8; row++) {
                for (let col = 0; col < 8; col++) {
                    if (board[row][col] === kingChar) {
                        return { row, col };
                    }
                }
            }
            return null;
        }

        // Check if a square is attacked
        function isSquareAttacked(row, col, byWhite) {
            for (let r = 0; r < 8; r++) {
                for (let c = 0; c < 8; c++) {
                    const piece = board[r][c];
                    if (piece && isWhitePiece(piece) === byWhite) {
                        if (canPieceAttack(piece, r, c, row, col)) {
                            return true;
                        }
                    }
                }
            }
            return false;
        }

        // Check if a piece can attack a square
        function canPieceAttack(piece, fromRow, fromCol, toRow, toCol) {
            if (fromRow === toRow && fromCol === toCol) return false;

            const pieceType = piece.toUpperCase();
            const rowDiff = Math.abs(toRow - fromRow);
            const colDiff = Math.abs(toCol - fromCol);

            switch (pieceType) {
                case 'K':
                    return rowDiff <= 1 && colDiff <= 1;
                case 'Q':
                    return (fromRow === toRow || fromCol === toCol || rowDiff === colDiff) && 
                           isPathClear(fromRow, fromCol, toRow, toCol);
                case 'R':
                    return (fromRow === toRow || fromCol === toCol) && 
                           isPathClear(fromRow, fromCol, toRow, toCol);
                case 'B':
                    return rowDiff === colDiff && isPathClear(fromRow, fromCol, toRow, toCol);
                case 'N':
                    return (rowDiff === 2 && colDiff === 1) || (rowDiff === 1 && colDiff === 2);
                case 'P':
                    const direction = isWhitePiece(piece) ? -1 : 1;
                    return rowDiff === 1 && colDiff === 1 && (toRow - fromRow) === direction;
            }
            return false;
        }

        // Check if king is in check
        function isKingInCheck(isWhite) {
            const king = findKing(isWhite);
            if (!king) return false;
            return isSquareAttacked(king.row, king.col, !isWhite);
        }

        // Check for checkmate
        function isCheckmate() {
            // Must be in check
            if (!isKingInCheck(false)) return false;

            // Check if any black piece has a legal move
            for (let fromRow = 0; fromRow < 8; fromRow++) {
                for (let fromCol = 0; fromCol < 8; fromCol++) {
                    const piece = board[fromRow][fromCol];
                    if (piece && !isWhitePiece(piece)) {
                        for (let toRow = 0; toRow < 8; toRow++) {
                            for (let toCol = 0; toCol < 8; toCol++) {
                                if (isValidMove(piece, fromRow, fromCol, toRow, toCol)) {
                                    // Try the move
                                    const captured = board[toRow][toCol];
                                    board[toRow][toCol] = piece;
                                    board[fromRow][fromCol] = null;

                                    const stillInCheck = isKingInCheck(false);

                                    // Undo
                                    board[fromRow][fromCol] = piece;
                                    board[toRow][toCol] = captured;

                                    if (!stillInCheck) return false;
                                }
                            }
                        }
                    }
                }
            }

            return true;
        }

        // Show status message
        function showStatus(message, type) {
            const statusEl = document.getElementById('status');
            statusEl.textContent = message;
            statusEl.className = `status ${type}`;
        }

        // Show checkmate celebration
        function showCheckmate() {
            showStatus("🎉 CHECKMATE! 🎉", "success");

            const attemptsText = moveAttempts === 1 ? 
                "Perfect! You found it on your first try!" : 
                `You solved it in ${moveAttempts} attempts.`;

            document.getElementById('successMessage').textContent = attemptsText;
            document.getElementById('overlay').classList.add('show');
        }

        // Close overlay
        function closeOverlay() {
            document.getElementById('overlay').classList.remove('show');
        }

        // Go to next scenario
        function nextScenario() {
            closeOverlay();
            const next = currentScenario < 3 ? currentScenario + 1 : 1;
            loadScenario(next);
        }

        // Start the app
        init();
    </script>
</body>
</html>
```

## Features

### 3 Mate-in-1 Scenarios:
1. **Back Rank Mate** - Classic pattern where the rook delivers mate on the 8th rank while the king is trapped by its own pawns
2. **Queen Delivery Mate** - The queen delivers checkmate to a cornered king blocked by its own pawns  
3. **King & Rook Coordination** - The king and rook work together to trap the enemy king on the edge

### Interactive Features:
- **Drag & Drop** - Drag white pieces to make moves
- **Valid Move Highlighting** - Green dots show where you can legally move
- **Scenario Selection** - Click buttons to switch between puzzles
- **Reset Button** - Start the current puzzle over

### Visual Feedback:
- **Success Animation** - Trophy celebration overlay when you find checkmate
- **Error Messages** - Red shake animation for wrong moves
- **Last Move Highlighting** - Yellow squares show the last move made
- **Move Counter** - Tracks how many attempts you've made

### How to Use:
1. Select a scenario (1, 2, or 3)
2. Read the hint in the description
3. Drag a white piece to deliver checkmate
4. If wrong, the move is undone with feedback
5. When correct, celebrate and try the next puzzle!
